{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1550081-which-antideuvlians-do-you-think-are-still-active","id":1550081,"title":"Which antideuvlians do you think are still active?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-12T16:02:15-07:00","id":1550081,"title":"Which antideuvlians do you think are still active?","content":"We know that methsaulth's like Helena, Kenminstri and some others have pretended to be younger and less powerful neonates and even anciliea.<br /> <br /> So it stands to reason that the 3rd generation wouldn't be doing the same and following their own interests and sometimes shaking there heads with some of the stories that they are directing whichever clan for there own purposes.<br /> <br /> I can see Toreador, Ventrue, Tziscme and perhaps Haqim still around and not in torpor or becoming something different like Gangrel or Malkav. So what antideuvlians do you think are still active?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T23:58:10-07:00","id":1550093,"title":"","content":"Define &quot;active&quot; :3<br /> Some are sleeping or sealed, some transcended or moved other parts of exsitence<br /> <br /> <b>Veddhartha</b> - The Venture Antediluvian, some sources says was destroyed by the Brujah Antediluvian/team of Brujah in the either first or either second city, yet he embraces left and right, till 60 BC when he embraced Antonius and Erik Eigermann/Ueruic and Danava believe themselves to be the guardians of their Antediluvian (pitri, or &quot;father&quot;), whom they call Veddhartha. These Danava claim that the Ventrue are in fact an errant antitribu bloodline of the Danava.<br /> So the best is at the moment, he is sleeping and the Danava are gurding his torpid body<br /> <br /> <b>Ilyes</b> - the Brujah Antediluvan diableire by Troile is not that certain; not even the date or explained the fact why the others not punished her (after all, the first diablerie of an Antediluvan - back than just an elder - would set up a dangerous precedent if not punished)<br /> So Troile is either Ilyes, whos mind shattered by the experience and emotions or as per Gehenna sourcbook says Ilyes hurled himself to the Future at the moment of his Diablerie and landed in Lilith's Garden<br /> <br /> <b>Troile</b> - IF she is not Ilyes, then she in torpor trapped under Carthage ruins hugging Moloch, sealed by a powerful ritual devised by Cybelle<br /> <br /> <b>Laza Omri Baras</b> - the Lasombra Antediluvian died, bot got better. in theory he was eaten by a flock of rebels, lead by Grationo... yet nobody can recall the exact event, and Grationo never claimed the &quot;throne&quot; nor able to recal the events (they were totally dominated) nor became a 3rd generation vampire. All and all, the Lasombra Antediluvian became an Abyssal Entity when he entered the Qlippoth of Primodial Darkness<br /> <br /> <b>Sutekh</b> - Vanished 33 AD. Lurking in Duat... but the Ventrue Nasch, the Circassian came upon a cult known as the Coil of the Lion that allegedly harbored the torpid body of the Antediluvian in the 14th century. When Nasch opened the sarcophagus that held the body, the last thing he heard was the sound of a thousand serpents rending the air with their unearthly hissing as the chamber around him vanished into blackness. He found himself standing upon a dais in a vast, open temple situated on an otherwise empty expanse of desert that stretched into infinity. Before him lay the body of a man with the head of an unspeakable beast, no sarcophagus in sight, naked but for a simple loincloth. Nasch managed to drink from the torpid creature, but the experience overwhelmed him and sent him to Torpor for more than a decade<br /> Actually the two version is not mutually exclusive, it is possible he is in Duat an the Coil of the Lion is guarding a portal<br /> <br /> <b>Set, the Snake</b><br /> Set I think is not actually Sutekh, but a seperate Antediluvian who been active in the Second City<br /> Simply what we know about Set from other clan's stories not really fit the Sutekh story<br /> Set, the Snake, brother of Arikel, Saulot, Malkav, Malakai and Nahema was quie philosophical, but agressive. Had his little talk with Malkav, argument, that led Saulot's departure to seek enlightenment and Answers, and with Absimilliard he cut out and ate his sister's, Arikel's heart and got banished from the City. And basically thats all. No real connection to the Followers or anything that would tie him to the Children of Rebellion. Just thougth it is interesting to mention. he may be still active and alive if he existed at all<br /> <br /> <b>Saulot </b>- Tremere ate him. Then he got better. The P'o of Saulot became the White Worm of Vienna, the Hun visited Hunedoara Castle and the Inconnu, then wandered away<br /> <br /> <b>Sargon </b>- The Cappadocian Antediluvan bacame a Wraith after Augustus tried to eat him, then In Giovanni Chronicles IV: Nuova Malattia, the Children of Isaac tried to put him to rest with a ritual from Marianna. Partially worked. During Gehenna, his soul was consumed when the Sixth Great Maelstrom hit the Shadowlands and became a Specter, a de-facto part of Oblivion.<br /> <br /> <b>Malkav</b> - After the fall of the Second City, Malkav is believed to have traveled towards the city of Petra. It is along this journey that some think the Eldest Malkavian was attacked and torn asunder. Malkav has likely become the Madness Network, a psychic link connecting virtually all members of Clan Malkavian. However, other accounts state that the Malkavian Antediluvian continues to sleep under Petra, or that he rests beneath Jerusalem... but it turned out, it is his twin sister, Malakai<br /> <br /> <b>Malakai </b>- Some scriptures (Beckett's Jyhad Diary, Gehenna and in \u200bThe Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra) claim he had a twin sister, Malakai, Black Hand scriptures say Malakai is imprisoned deep within the Shadowlands because she is so mad and powerful that she warps reality around her. (Malakai is mentioned in the Shaal Fragment as an antediluvian who seeks &quot;peace&quot; during the first Gehenna. However, since Arikel is said to seek unity, the peace Malakai seeks may not be diplomatic in nature. Rather, she could have sought peace by journeying to the Shadowlands or entering Torpor.)<br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary suggest, she sleeps under Jerusalem<br /> <br /> <b>Nahema </b>- Chaining the Beast mentions one branch of the Path of Lilith, the Path of Awakening. The followers of it believes that Arikel and Malkav were twins, children of Lilith, and that they had a younger sister, Nahema, who also received the Embrace. According to legend, Nahema descended into Hell, but never lost touch with her siblings, her spirit forever bound to them and their childer \u2013 it is Nahema's spirit that whispers in the Malkavian Madness Network, that burns in the hearts of the Toreador. Some of her worshippers call her the Dark Muse, the Anti-Muse, and the Demon Queen of Madness, and she is said to be patron saint of serial killers and torturers<br /> <br /> <b>The Eldest </b>- masquerading as Lugoj, let his body be transported to a hidden crypt beneath what would become New York City by Zantosa Revenants that knew of his ruse. There, it entered a meditative state to reach Metamorphosis. In the process, its body dissolved to a puddle of slime, then transformed into fungi, then into plants and every other living creature in existence, exploring the infinitude of life by assuming its shape. It started to infuse itself into other creatures, beginning with plants and animals, to master them and unite all Creation into itself. The Eldest appears to have had more trouble than it should in its quest, lost in itself looking for an answer it could not find, riven by the loss of its true bonds to the Earth. Eventually, sometime in the early 21st century, it found its way back to itself, then left New York to seek its siblings' counsel<br /> <br /> <b>Haqim </b>- The last time anyone has seen the Banu Haqim Antediluvian was in the British Isles in 121 CE, where he was engaged in philosophical conversations with the Ventrue Prince of London, Mithras - which is interesting by itself, since Mithras would be diablerized in 1996 by one of Haqim's own descendants...\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <b>Absimiliard</b>. - The time the Nosferatu Antediluvian fell in torpor, he was fighting Baba Yaga in Russia milleniums ago. Has spent a long time in torpor at Enoch, but he probably awoke recently in Eastern European mountains. [Cb-To] has him and Arikel meeting in 2nd century Rome. He has planned a nuclear attack in 2000, but with a little help of Kupala, that was avoided. According Gehenna, he retreated back under the Atlentic Ocean to breed Kaiju-like monsters<br /> <br /> <b>Arikel </b>and <b>Ishtar - </b>the Toreador Antediluvians are interesting.<br /> As for Arikel, the Toreador scholars claim that their clan's Antediluvian was killed in the time of Enoch by the plotting of Absimiliard and Set, who supposedly cut out and ate her heart. Yet, there are records that indicate that she had not experienced Final Death, and had awakened from Torpor around 260 BCE, acting as an advisor to Prince Alchias.<br /> Ishtar tried to take the Tablet of Destiny from either Ennoia or either Enkidu Outraged by this action, Ennoia set out to kill the Toreador Antediluvian and tracked Ishtar to Sumer. Ishtar fled but not before unleashing upon them some great monster known as the Bull of Heaven, while she escaped to Crete. In Crete, Ishtar resided with King Minos, who desired and demanded her gift. Initially, she refused, but then compromised to embrace his son. Unworthy of the embrace, the son fell into the clutches of the Beast. His erratic behavior had him imprisoned by his father Minos, in what was an underground maze.<br /> Both of the Toreador Antediluvians went off the map, but were in Greece<br /> Worth to mention, there is a Toreador bloodline/Laibon Legacy called the Ishatrri claim to be descended from the Babylonian goddess Ishtar, they are the only Laibon Legacy that are not native to Africa; however, through manipulation and diplomacy, they have become an important part of Laibon culture.<br /> <br /> <b>Ennoia -</b> It is suggested that Ennoia fell into a long torpor around the time of Christ and there is debate as to whether she has woken up from it yet.<br /> <br /> <b>Zapatashura</b> - His death was described in deatail, and considered dead, yet even in V5 there are hints (blood of Zapatashura) maybe he is not THAT dead<br /> Like how Malkav was tore apart, yet his children consumed his blood to shiled it from the sun, so he survived as the Cobweb/Madnes network... if that trick worked with Malkav, Zapatashura may survived too, since the Sun not destroyed his lifeblood.... or it was just a reality alteration<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere </b>- after Saulot evicted him from his owm body (either in the dark ages, right after he tried to diablerize him - witch mean Saulot did a very dirty on his own clan - or in 1998) his spirit fled and is now in Goratrix body.\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b<br /> <b>Augustus</b> - lies in torpor in the Mausoleum, Venice. Then after V5, in pieces\u200b<br /> <br /> The <b>Apostates</b>\u200b <b>of Lilith </b>are a coterie of Antediluvians who not slumebred and actively been around (Malakai and Ilyes are here too, see them above)\u200b<br /> <b>Eickos</b>, also known as Narcise is the Crone so technically not a 3rd but a 2nd Generation vampire Embraced by Caine<br /> <b>Erinye </b>a wrathful avenger of the souls of the dead with a passing resemblance to the Lamia<br /> <b>Ikopabe</b>, a silent, bestial hunter, possible progenitor of the Akunanse<br /> <b>Lucian</b>, a preternaturally beautiful, charismatic, and narcissistic man, broodmate of Absimiliard - could be the same situation as Isthar and Arikel and he is a Nosferatu progenitor or at least the farther of the Guruhi and the Guruhi legend about the <i>other </i>Line is not the Nosferatu-Nictuku but the Nosferatu-Guruhi<br /> <b>Mekhet, </b>a Mummy-like blood sorcerer, possibly the First cursed with a rotting boddy like the Samedi have; like Lucian and Absimiliard or Arikel and Ishtar he may or may not the brood bother of Sargon aka. Cappadocius\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Sarah, the Shaper</b> was also introduced in Gehenna, she was around and quite active<br /> <br /> <br /> Erciyes Fragments states that there were more Cainites at the time of the Great Flood,and also suggests that the differences in generation came from a curse levied by Caine and did not appear until after his own childer were slain, so the second and the third were basically equal and possible everyone who been Embraced before the Flood<br /> <br /> <br /> And finally we have two wild cards so to speak:<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Dracian </b>(Clanbook: Ravnos Revised, World of Darkness: Gypsies)<br /> Dracian was the name of a thief that was Embraced by Irad in order to spy on the third generation. Irad suspected the other third generation neonates of plotting against the three members of the second generation and their sire. Dracian, for his part, took to the plot like a fish to water. He was at heart a selfish man, and becoming one of the typically selfish Cainite only deepened that trait.<br /> Buuuuut<br /> According to Roma lore, Dracian has been appointed as the creator of a tree that was the embodiment life and knowledge, full in its age and beauty. It is said that one of the golden fruits of this Tree of Knowledge could cure the eternal thirst for blood in a vampire (as well as bestowing other unknown gifts). Some sources claim Dracian to be a member of the second Generation, Embraced by Caine himself during his wanderings and the sire of the Ravnos Antediluvian and Ennoia, who betrayed him and was cast out of the First City as a result.<br /> He is a maybe 2nd generation, and wandered to the East, like many others... Amriat allegedly destroyed him<br /> <br /> <b>Amriat</b><i> (</i>World of Darkness: Gypsies)<br /> He is a maybe 2nd generation, and allegedly destroyed Dracian in his desire to take the Tree of Knowledge and its fruit for himself.<br /> Like Dracian could be a 3rd Generation vampire. It is a bit murky.\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> And finally<br /> Who is/was <b>Typhon</b>?<br /> According to Gehenna, one of the 23 Antediluvians (p. 154)<br /> <br /> Thank you for coming<br /> <br /> But the answer is a bit... more complicated, considering Gehenna: Time of Judgment is a bit soft-canon, more like a What if...? and ideas than hard facts<br /> <br /> What we know about him is from the <b>Isis Fragments </b>(World of Darkness: Mummy Second Edition, p. 16-21)<br /> In that he was stranger that came on the night of a full moon, presenting himself at their court and beseeching an audience with Osiris.<br /> It is said that Typhon was cold, not only in manner but in body, and although his beauty was breathtaking, the only emotion that crossed his fine, pale features was a cruel humor.<br /> In Osiris' court, Typhon warned the ruler of Egypt about the imminent conflict that would sweep throughout the land if they were unprepared.<br /> For four moons this pattern continued, as Typhon would reappear on the eve of a full moon to speak privately with Osiris, and every time he did so, the king grew filled with quiet dread. On the morning of Typhon's fourth and final departure, Osiris was found ill and near death, pale and bloodless on his bedchamber floor. They later discovered that he had been embraced as one of the kindred.<br /> <br /> Now Osiris is belived to be a 4th generation and in Cairo by Night it was said:<br /> Osiris was reported to manifest the &quot;vigor of a thousand bulls&quot; (likely a reference to either Fortitude or Potence), the &quot;movement of the desert winds&quot; (Celerity) and the &quot;sudden irresistible power of his speech&quot; (likely referring to Dominate or Presence ) after his Embrace<br /> <br /> This narrows a bit down<br /> <br /> One candiate is <b>Ilyies</b>, the original Antediluvian of the <i>Learned Clan</i><br /> The discipline set fits and intersting to mention Osiris is described as becoming cold and cruel.. like a True Brujah<br /> And later he developed Bardo a discipline that requires rigid asceticism and strict self-discipline and meditation - again a very True Brujah like thing<br /> Clan Book: Tzimisce Rev. mentions:<br /> Mekhet was a sibling of [Tzimisce] (and thus possibly another childe of Ynosh/Enoch) who, with [Brujah], &quot;played shadow games with mortals, delighting in their own cunning and agendas&quot;.<br /> This again, fit the Isis Freagments description &quot;Typhon was cold, not only in manner but in body, and although his beauty was breathtaking, the only emotion that crossed his fine, pale features was a cruel humor.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yet there is <i>another </i>candidate and I don't actually managed to find the source of this &quot;rumor&quot; - and if anyone know who and from where it started I would greatly appreciate it!<br /> The other is the <b>Lasombra Antedulivan </b>\u200b<br /> Lasombra had interests in Africa, Ontai/Montano was a Massai (who inhabiting northern, central and southern Kenya and northern Tanzania, near the African Great Lakes region - more or less was&quot;neigbours&quot; of Egypt ) and another of his Child's name mentioned in Clan Lasombra Trilogy 2: Shadows Tepelit have a Maasai name too<br /> The vigor of a thousand bulls (Potance) and sudden irresistible power of his speech&quot; (Dominate) also fits and with a stretch the movement of the desert winds could be interpreted as entering a shadow and steping out from another that looked like speed... (but I must admit it is a great stretch - and no one tought Osiris how to use Obtenebration)<br /> The cruel humor and cold mannerism also a very Lasombra-like trait<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 04-13-2025, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}